    many stay active — one that never fires can be removed",
  experiment_B("perturbation"): "anomalous climatic input ⟹ do the modes
    adjust (plasticity)? return when E normalizes (memory)? same convergence
    time (stable drift)?",

  risks: {
    instability:  "modes oscillate ⟹ decreasing lr(t) = lr₀/(1 + t/T)
                   — converges by Robbins-Monro 1951",
    collapse:     "∀ μₛ converge to one ⟹ repulsion penalty
                   L_collapse = Σ_{s≠t} max(0, d_min − ‖μₛ − μₜ‖²)",
    catastrophic: "the system forgets how to be viable ⟹ (1) freeze modes when
                   λ > 0 ▪ (2) checkpoint μₛ_design to revert ▪ (3) raise τ
